    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. step 3 and 4 seem a bit vague though. can you get more specific about the actual technical rollout? like, how should we handle the actual registration process per user, and what's the best way to manage the lifecycle of the keys (if someone loses one or leaves the firm)? also, how do we ensure we aren't leaving any gaps in security during the migration period?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, let's delve deeper into the technical aspects:\n\n3. Detailed User Onboarding:\n   - Host an all-hands meeting to introduce the new MFA, addressing why Yubikeys are superior in security.\n   - Distribute in-depth guides and examples on YubiKey setup for different operating systems (Windows/macOS/iOS for iPhones/Android devices).\n   - Create a FAQ document for common issues and how to address them, helping with the initial setup and troubleshooting.\n\n4. Technical Rollout and Lifecycle Management:\n   - Registration Process: Establish a dedicated portal using Authy, Okta, or Duo's integration. Guide each employee through registering their Yubikey there, which also logs the unique fingerprints of the security keys for device authentication.\n   - Key Management: Enforce a card-index system to track key allocation and retirements. This can be linked to an employee directory. In case a Yubikey is lost, prompt for an immediate change of the key and replace it if necessary.\n   - Migration Security: During the switchover, maintain dual factors (password + SMS) temporarily. After confirming stability, phase out SMS factor. Conduct in-depth security audits to ensure no gaps in security during the transition.\n   -",
      "source": "target",
